      "say": "For words that end in y, look at the letter just before the y. If it's a consonant, the y changes to ies: baby, babies. [click] If it's a vowel, a, e, o, u, just add s: boy, boys. [click] And words ending in f or fe usually change to ves: knife, knives. Usually, not always: roof, roofs.",
      "teach": "The vowel test is the whole of the y rule, so say the five vowels out loud. Words ending in -o also vary (tomato → tomatoes but photo → photos); mention them in one spoken sentence at most and keep them off the screen.",
