      "say": "Line one: the spelling rules. Most nouns add s. Hissing sounds add es, and you can hear the extra syllable. A consonant before y makes ies. [click] Line two: the irregular words have no rule, so learn them as pairs. Man, men. Child, children. Person, people. And women sounds like wi-min. [click] Line three, the one that matters most for a Mongolian speaker: after any number bigger than one, the noun must change. Three books, never three book. Close: Now you can count and talk about more than one of anything, and say the ending so that people actually hear it. [click] Closing line (spoken, never on the slide): Одоо энэ видеоны доорх дасгалаар мэдлэгээ шалгаарай. Hold the slide silently for three seconds.",
      "teach": "On line three, lengthen the final s of books slightly so it is unmistakable. Hold the slide silently for three seconds after the closing sentence.",
